SOURCE VERIFICATION (Maven Central sources jars, re-confirmed 2026-07-15):
  * 2.2.6 ObjectSerializationDecoder.doDecode(): `in.setMatchers(acceptMatchers); out.write(in.getObject(classLoader));`
    -- so the TCP decoder path IS the acceptMatchers+getObject sink. ObjectSerializationCodecFactory.accept(Pattern)
    -> decoder.accept -> acceptMatchers.
  * 2.2.6 AbstractIoBuffer.getObject.resolveClass(): clazz==null (type-0) -> Class.forName(name,false,cl) NO allowlist;
    else (type-1) -> loop acceptMatchers, throw ClassNotFoundException if not found. => type-0/null-clazz RESIDUAL open.
  * 2.2.7 AbstractIoBuffer.getObject.resolveClass(): checks acceptMatchers FIRST for ANY class before Class.forName
    (covers null-clazz); readClassDescriptor()'s type-1 path likewise checks before Class.forName. => residual closed.
  * 2.2.3 decoder has NO accept()/setMatchers and resolveClass returns any class (type-1 `return clazz`, type-0
    Class.forName). => unrestricted; reflection accept() no-ops.

